#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# prime_zeta_p

#% text
# `prime_zeta_p(s)` is the prime zeta function, the sum of `p^-s` over the primes `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is evaluated for inexact `s` with real part above 1, by the series `sum over k of moebius_mu(k)/k log(zeta(k s))`; `n(prime_zeta_p(2), 30)` gives 30 digits.

#% item
# An exact argument stays unevaluated until `n` is applied.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
prime_zeta_p(2.)
#% output
#= 0.45224742004106544

#% cell
n(prime_zeta_p(2), 30)
#% output
#= 0.452247420041065498506543364832248

#% cell
prime_zeta_p(1.5 + 2.*im)
#% output
#= -0.13197927923571662 - 0.42464346272670406im

#% cell
n(prime_zeta_p(3))
#% output
#= 0.1747626392994435

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `zeta`, `moebius_mu`, `prime`
